      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14152648/assets/7dca3b5a6206733052e8f74139ca4d0cc7d6cd38d8553b1736580c5eed0c64a6.png)\n\nSteven is making french bread. The amount of water he needs for a given amount of flour is given in the graph above. In its simplest form, what is the ratio of flour to water?",
      "worked_solution": "One of the points belonging to the graph is $(24,10).$\n\nLet's write the ratio $24:10$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{24}{10}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this fraction by dividing both the numerator and the denominator by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{24÷2}{10÷2} & =\\frac{12}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the ratio of flour to water is $12:5$",
